          </p>

          <p>
            Output matters more than most buyers expect. A full-size refrigerator draws only 100 to 200 watts while running, but its compressor can pull several times that for a moment at start-up. A microwave, a space heater or a hair dryer can sit near or above 1,500 watts continuously. The C300X cannot run any of those, the C800 Plus manages some of them, and the C1000 handles nearly all household appliances one at a time. Only the F3800 family can run a 240V load such as a well pump or a dryer circuit, and even then you should check the motor's starting current before counting on it.
          </p>

          <p>
            Weight is the other number worth knowing before you click buy. Anker lists the C300X at roughly 9 pounds, light enough to toss in a backpack. The C1000 is close to 28 pounds, comfortable for one person to move between rooms but not something you will carry far. The F3800 is about 132 pounds and rolls on wheels; it lives in a garage or utility room and moves only when it has to. If you plan to camp with it, weight caps your choice before capacity does.
          </p>
