          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
            10. Common Mistakes to Avoid
          </h2>

          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying the C300 DC by mistake</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                The C300 DC and C300X look alike in photos, but the DC version has no AC outlets. If you need to run a fan, a CPAP with a standard plug, or lights with a wall plug, confirm the listing says C300X and shows AC outlets before you check out, or you will be making a return.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Sizing by capacity and ignoring output</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A large battery does not help if the inverter cannot start your load. A refrigerator, sump pump or microwave can exceed what a small unit delivers at start-up. Compare each appliance's running and starting watts against the AC output rating, not just the watt-hours, before choosing between the C800 Plus and C1000.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Treating the F3800 as portable</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                At about 132 pounds, the F3800 rolls across a garage floor but does not go up stairs or into a truck bed easily. People who buy it for camping usually regret it. If you need both camping and home backup, a C1000 with an expansion battery is often the better combination.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Backfeeding a panel without a transfer switch</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Running a cord from an F3800 into a dryer outlet to power the house is dangerous to you and to utility workers. Circuit-level backup needs a transfer switch, an interlock kit or Anker's home power panel, installed by a licensed electrician. Budget for that work when you price the system.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying an old NMC PowerHouse on sale</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Some older Anker PowerHouse units use NMC cells rated for far fewer cycles than LFP. They turn up cheap on clearance and in used listings. Unless the listing clearly says LiFePO4 or LFP, assume it is an older chemistry and buy a current SOLIX model instead.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

